<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What kessler needs beyond the hardened runtime, for bundle/notarize.sh.

  Only one thing: kessler talks to Music.app through osascript (import, and
  asking Music which tracks it already has). The osascript it starts counts
  as kessler, and under the hardened runtime an app may only send Apple
  Events with this entitlement; without it Music answers -1743 and nothing
  happens.

  Not needed, and so not here:
  - audio output (rodio/cpal): playing sound asks nothing; only recording
    would (com.apple.security.device.audio-input), and kessler records nothing.
  - network, curl as a child process, files on the iPod or anywhere else:
    the app is not sandboxed (no com.apple.security.app-sandbox), so none of
    the sandbox's network or file entitlements apply. curl and osascript are
    Apple's own signed tools.
  - JIT, unsigned executable memory, disabled library validation: kessler
    loads no code at run time and no library from outside the system.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
